WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.762
Machine learning brings together many ideas from this course.

00:00:03.762 --> 00:00:06.912
Python gives us the programming foundation.

00:00:06.912 --> 00:00:14.022
NumPy and Pandas give us arrays, Data frames, vectors, and numerical representations.

00:00:14.022 --> 00:00:17.567
Data cleaning helps us improve input quality.

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:24.105
Statistics and visualization help us understand distributions and relationships before modeling.

00:00:24.685 --> 00:00:32.302
Machine learning adds a new goal: learning a relationship from examples so we can make predictions for new cases.

00:00:32.302 --> 00:00:37.372
That means the work you have already done is not separate from machine learning.

00:00:37.372 --> 00:00:45.347
It is the foundation. Next semester, you will learn more algorithms and more advanced evaluation techniques.

00:00:45.347 --> 00:00:52.972
But those methods will be much easier to understand if you already know what features are, how data becomes numeric,

00:00:52.972 --> 00:00:59.076
why we separate training from testing, and why model evaluation must use unseen data.
